  "user_request_original": "Design a 21-layer Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate with Air incident medium using Ta2O5 and SiO2. Layer sequence: Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2 (layers 1-6 fixed QWOT) | Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2 (layers 7-10 optimizable) | Ta2O5 cavity (layer 11 fixed at 360.0 nm) | SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O2 (layers 12-15 optimizable) | SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O5/SiO2/Ta2O5 (layers 16-21 fixed QWOT). Initialize fixed QWOT layers: Ta2O5 at 184.5 nm, SiO2 at 267.2 nm (quarter-wave at 1550 nm). Optimize layers 7-10 and 12-15 with bounds 50-450 nm. Evaluate transmittance spectrum from 1400-1700 nm. Target: maximize T at 1550 nm, suppress T in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 5 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs, one cavity layer, and exactly 5 reverse-order pairs (21 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on fused silica with a fixed 360 nm Ta2O5 cavity, optimizing eight intermediate layers between 1400–1700 nm to maximize transmittance at 1550 nm while suppressing it in adjacent bands.",
